 "A **locked** level tells you how many levels away it is.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "A **village** is twelve boards on the map. A **chapter** is twenty levels, used for chapter badges and Game Center achievements. They are counted separately, so a chapter can end in the middle of a village.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "A timed gift; the badge counts down to when it is ready.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "A weekly story: clear four village finales to rescue a friend.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Accessibility pieces are always free.": "help:friends-and-wardrobe",
 "All Villages: filters for All 167, In progress, Completed and Locked; a heading for First Light, villages 1 to 28, with 217 of 1,008 stars; and village cards with their levels and stars, such as Cherry Blossom Town, levels 205 to 216, 9 of 36 stars, marked You are here, and Spaceport Gardens, which unlocks when level 216 is cleared.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "An opt-in contest for up to 100 players. Shares your player name when you join.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Any of these can be switched off in **Settings › Game › Game features**, along with offers on the map.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Brick Royale": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Chests, gifts and other things on the map": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Choose or hide your **flag** in your Profile.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Clearing a whole village shows a celebration card with **Share** and **On we go**.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Collecting stars climbs the village’s star ladder: 50 coins, a Hint, 100 coins and a Rocket. A badge on the map tells you when a reward is ready to claim.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Crew Race": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Day-streak rewards": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Days in a row": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Each **season** has **30 tiers**. Clearing new levels climbs them; Hard clears count one extra and Super Hard two.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Each board can earn up to three stars, so a village holds 36. The **stars** pill in the header shows how many you have in this village.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Events and races": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Events come and go on a calendar and show as a banner on Home and a badge on the Journey. Some double or triple the coins for a clear. Four kinds of race and rescue run alongside:": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Every 100 after": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Every element on the map offers **Where am I** and **Go to my next level**; the two-finger double tap speaks your village, levels cleared and next level; and a three-finger swipe moves a village at a time. See [Playing with VoiceOver](help:voiceover#journey).": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Every pass and timed item is a one-time purchase. **Nothing in OutBrick is a subscription**, and nothing renews by itself.": "help:shop-and-purchases",
 "Every village is built from toy bricks in its own theme, and repeats of a theme come back at a different time of day or season, so no two villages look the same.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Five new levels in a day, against players and friends.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Floats by now and then. An optional video catches it for coins or a short free-booster window.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Friend Rescue": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Friends, the Collection and the Wardrobe": "help:friends-and-wardrobe",
 "How the map of 2,000 levels works: villages and chapters, stars and village rewards, chests and gifts, the atlas of every village, and replaying a board.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Leaders and Game Center": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Little hidden things to find along the way. Tap anything that looks out of place.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Meet the nine brick friends, see what they do on Home and on the board, and how your Profile, the Collection and the Wardrobe work.": "help:friends-and-wardrobe",
 "Missed a day? A streak of three days or more can be restored within a week, free with a streak saver or for 250 coins. You can hold up to two savers.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Nothing paid is offered on a board before level 6.": "help:shop-and-purchases",
 "On devices with Apple’s on-device language model, the friends can make up their own lines (**Settings › Game › Mascot AI chatter**). It runs entirely on your device.": "help:friends-and-wardrobe",
 "Open the **Shop** and scroll to the very bottom.": "help:shop-and-purchases · help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Outfits, board plates, palettes, brick finishes, celebrations, trails and frames.": "help:friends-and-wardrobe · help:meet-the-friends",
 "Prefer a quieter map? Settings › Game › **Game features** lets you hide events and offers you are not interested in. Nothing you have earned is lost.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Premium tiers you have already reached are paid the moment you unlock it.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Prices are shown in your own currency by the App Store.": "help:shop-and-purchases",
 "Purchases are made through Apple, so Apple handles refunds: see [our refunds page](/refunds) for how to ask. If something you bought did not arrive, try **Restore Purchase** first, then write to us privately with the [contact form](/contact). Never post a receipt or order number in the community.": "help:shop-and-purchases",
 "Race four players through a village. Shares your player name.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Refunds and problems with a purchase": "help:shop-and-purchases",
 "Remove Ads and the Brick Pass": "help:shop-and-purchases · help:rewards-and-ads",
 "Restore brings back everything you own for good: **Remove Ads**, Brick Pass seasons 1 to 3 and Wardrobe items. Coins, boosters, lives and other things you use up are not restored by the App Store; they travel with your progress through iCloud instead. See [Progress, iCloud and privacy](help:progress-privacy-and-account).": "help:shop-and-purchases",
 "Restoring purchases": "help:shop-and-purchases",
 "Rewards, events and the Brick Pass": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Secrets": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Shelves from top to bottom: **Special Offers** (the Starter Bundle while it lasts, the Piggy Bank, the Booster Pass, the Brick Pass and Remove Ads), the **Weekly Deal**, event offers during an event, the **Weekend Deal** from Friday to Monday, **Boosters & Moves**, **Boosters**, **Passes**, **Bundles**, **Lives**, the **Wardrobe**, **Coins**, and finally **Restore Purchase** and the legal links.": "help:shop-and-purchases",
 "Sign in to the iPhone with the same Apple Account you bought with, and to iCloud.": "help:shop-and-purchases",
 "Stars and village rewards": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Tap **Missions** on Home, or the Missions card on the Pass tab: three things to do today and three for the week, each with a reward. Finish one and tap **Claim**, or **Claim all**. Daily missions reset at midnight UTC; weekly ones on Monday.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "Tap **Restore Purchase**.": "help:shop-and-purchases · help:lost-progress-and-purchases",
 "Tap a chest on the path to see what it holds. When you reach it, the win card lists the coins and boosters it paid.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Tap your **current level** to play it. Tap any **cleared** level to replay it and improve its stars; replaying never moves your place on the map.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "Tap your avatar on Home or the Journey. Change your name and avatar, choose your country flag (automatic, a country you pick, or hidden), open the Collection and see your stats: first-try wins, boards beaten under target, best streak, total clears, moves and more. The game’s version number is at the foot; quote it when you [report a bug](help:reporting-bugs).": "help:friends-and-wardrobe",
 "The **Brick Wheel** button on Home gives one free spin a day, for coins (50 to 500) or a Hint, Rocket or UFO. Clear three new levels in a day and the free spin pays double coins. An optional video gives a second spin.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "The **Free** track pays coins and boosters to everyone.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "The **Leaders** tab unlocks at level 21: one all-time board of players, with flags. Tap **Show more** to see further down.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "The **My level** pin brings you back to where you are.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "The **Piggy Bank** fills with coins as you clear new levels; you can open it for a small price when it is ready.": "help:shop-and-purchases",
 "The **Premium** track, unlocked by buying that season’s Brick Pass, adds bigger rewards. Owning it also adds three lives to your tank, three free moves at the out-of-moves screen, and takes away videos: rewards are claimed without watching.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "The Brick Pass": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "The Brick Wheel": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "The Collection": "help:friends-and-wardrobe · help:meet-the-friends",
 "The Collection opens at level 95, from your Profile or the Pass tab. It holds **Brick Cards**, **Chapter Badges** for each chapter you finish, **Keepsakes** and **Seasonal Cards**: a card every third new level, nine to a season. Spare Sparks can be exchanged for a missing card.": "help:friends-and-wardrobe",
 "The Daily Brick and day streaks": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "The Daily Brick and day streaks, the Brick Wheel, Missions, the Brick Pass, events and races, and the leaderboard.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "The Journey and its villages": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "The Journey has **2,000 levels** in **167 villages** of twelve boards each (the final village has eight).": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "The Journey is one long, brick-built boulevard. Your current level glows.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "The Journey map: a cobbled path climbing through a village of pink blossom trees, with level stops 213, 214 and 215. Level 214 glows with a Play label. Badges run down both sides.": "help:journey-and-villages",
 "The Pass tab. Every clear moves you up the season’s 30 tiers.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "The Pass tab: a season header, a Missions card and a Collection card, then two columns of rewards, Free and Premium, climbing through numbered tiers.": "help:rewards-and-events",
 "The Shop, purchases and restoring": "help:shop-and-purchases",
